<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="MIPS:BE:32:default:default">
<!--
    kuna loader (dynrelocs, always on), GH-904: same-image calls and
    data accesses through a MIPS PIC GOT.

    A MIPS dynamic image relocates its primary GOT with no relocation
    records: the dynamic linker adds the load bias to the local entries and
    stores each defined dynamic symbol's address in its global entry.  The
    loader marked only the import stubs' slots constant, so a call to a
    function the image defines and every global or static variable read
    through the GOT stayed a load of a variable slot:
        v2 = (*dat_1043c)();                               (bug, c_add)
        *(int4 *)(dat_10428 + 0x458) = *(int4 *)(dat_10428 + 0x458) + 1;
        v2 = (*v1)();                                      (bug, c_calls)
    Those slots already hold their run-time values at the link-time
    addresses kuna maps the image at, so they are now constant too and the
    call names add64, the weak wfn, and the reads name counter and gdata.

    Stage: P1 program prep (loader constant ranges).  Single pass; the loader
    facts are checked by
    decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/verify_dynrelocs_gate.rs.

    Image: decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/mipsgot_gcc_be.so
    (mipsgot.c); see mipsgot.provenance.

    Assert #1: c_add calls add64 and stores to sink64.
    Assert #2: c_calls bumps counter, calls wfn and reads gdata.
    Assert #3: no call goes through a GOT slot any more.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">03e0000800000000</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/mipsgot_gcc_be.so</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>lo fu c_add</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu c_calls</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="mipsgot-local #1: c_add calls add64" min="1" max="1">= add64\(</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="mipsgot-local #1b: c_add stores to sink64" min="1" max="2">sink64</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="mipsgot-local #2: c_calls bumps counter" min="1" max="1">counter \+= 1;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="mipsgot-local #2b: c_calls calls wfn and reads gdata" min="1" max="1">wfn\(.*gdata|gdata.*wfn\(</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="mipsgot-local #3: no call through a GOT slot" min="0" max="0">\(\*[^)]*dat_</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
